NovaBank: Advanced Database Systems Portfolio

Course: MIT 8103: Advanced Database Systems
Programme: Master of Information Technology (MIT)
Academic Session: 2026/2027
Assessment: First Semester Continuous Assessment

Project Overview

NovaBank is a simulated digital banking system created as part of the MIT 8103 Advanced Database Systems course.

The system will manage banking customers, accounts, transfers, and other financial activities. I chose a banking system as the domain for this project due to the need for banking systems to maintain accurate and secure data. For example, if a customer transfers ₦50,000 from their account to another customer’s account, the database must successfully complete that transfer. If the transfer cannot be completed, then the transaction must be undone (rolled back) to ensure that the customer’s money is not transferred to an account that they did not authorize.

There are five main areas of the database system covered in this portfolio.

Portfolio Activities
Database Design and Modelling

Design a PostgreSQL database for NovaBank with customers, accounts, transfers, and more. All tables must use appropriate primary and foreign keys, as well as being normalized up to Third Normal Form (3NF).
Query Processing and Optimisation

Use PostgreSQL to write queries that retrieve data from the NovaBank database, and analyze the performance of those queries using the EXPLAIN ANALYZE tool. Compare performance with and without indexing on the tables.
Transactions and Concurrency

Execute banking transactions while upholding the ACID properties of banking databases. Test the transactional features of PostgreSQL to ensure that transactions can be committed or rolled back, isolated from other transactions, and allow concurrent updates to accounts.
NoSQL and Advanced Data Models

Use MongoDB to store transaction activity records for NovaBank. Create sample NoSQL documents for transactions, and execute queries on those documents. Explain the situations where NoSQL databases are appropriate for banking systems.
Distributed and Cloud Databases

Set up a PostgreSQL database with a primary and replica instances in Docker. Examine the characteristics of distributed databases, including replication and availability.

Technologies
PostgreSQL: Relational database management system
MongoDB: NoSQL database system
Docker: Database containerization tool
SQL: Query language for relational databases
DBeaver/pgAdmin: Database management tools
GitHub: Code repository

